)$ for the following predicates: \n\n- $P(x):$ $x$ is odd.\n\n- $Q(x):$ $\\sqrt{x}$ is integer." :question/worked-solution "Since $P(x)⇒Q(x)≡¬P(x)∨Q(x),$ the corresponding truth sets can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P⇒Q} & ={T}_{¬P∨Q} \\\\  & ={T}_{¬P}\\cup {T}_{Q} \\\\  & ={\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cup {T}_{Q}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we note the following:\n\n- The truth set of $P(x)$ is \n\n$$\n{T}_{P}=\\{5,15,25,35\\}.\n$$\n\nAs a result, the complement is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\overset{―}{T}}_{P} & =\\overset{―}{\\{5,15,25,35\\}} \\\\  & =\\{10,20,30\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The truth set of $Q(x)$ is \n\n$$\n{T}_{Q}=\\{25\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P⇒Q} & ={\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cup {T}_{Q} \\\\  & =\\{10,20,30\\}\\cup \\{25\\} \\\\  & =\\{10,20,25,30\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186381645 :answer-field/correct "answer-d48c3def-d0f9-52d3-be15-de9c130118a6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d48c3def-d0f9-52d3-be15-de9c130118a6" "answer-91f26d38-d7ad-54b2-8893-934a3a454856" "answer-5826c839-6514-58d5-b7ad-37f4b9d17f20" "answer-4ebb999a-dcd7-59c8-ae67-e4b0d1b4ebb8" "answer-c7e4d5ce-7267-5b6d-8a25-095f9eebaa99"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d48c3def-d0f9-52d3-be15-de9c130118a6" :answer/id #uuid "d48c3def-d0f9-52d3-be15-de9c130118a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{10,20,25,30\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-91f26d38-d7ad-54b2-8893-934a3a454856" :answer/id #uuid "91f26d38-d7ad-54b2-8893-934a3a454856" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{10,20,30\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5826c839-6514-58d5-b7ad-37f4b9d17f20" :answer/id #uuid "5826c839-6514-58d5-b7ad-37f4b9d17f20" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{25\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4ebb999a-dcd7-59c8-ae67-e4b0d1b4ebb8" :answer/id #uuid "4ebb999a-dcd7-59c8-ae67-e4b0d1b4ebb8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{5,15,25,35\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c7e4d5ce-7267-5b6d-8a25-095f9eebaa99" :answer/id #uuid "c7e4d5ce-7267-5b6d-8a25-095f9eebaa99" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{5,15,35\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-28a2abe2-d607-5ca5-a1d6-25d691cd727c" :question/id #uuid "28a2abe2-d607-5ca5-a1d6-25d691cd727c" :question/math-academy-id "q-183378" :question/problem "Find the truth set of $P(x)⇔Q(x)$ given the following predicates defined over the universal set $R:$\n\n- $P(x):$ ${x}^{2}\\le 9$\n\n- $Q(x):$ $5x-3>7$" :question/worked-solution "Since we have that\n\n$$\nP(x)⇔Q(x)≡(P(x)∧Q(x))∨(¬P(x)∧¬Q(x)),\n$$\n\n \n\nthe corresponding truth set can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P⇔Q}=({T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q})\\cup ({\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we note the following:\n\n- To find the truth set of $P(x),$ we solve the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & \\le 9 \\\\ -3 & \\le x\\le 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the truth set of $P(x)$ is \n${T}_{P}=[-3,3].$ \nAs a result, the complement is\n${\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}=(-\\infty ,-3)\\cup (3,\\infty ).$\n\n- To find the truth set of $Q(x),$ we solve the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x-3 & >7 \\\\ 5x & >10 \\\\ x & >2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the truth set of $Q(x)$ is\n${T}_{Q}=(2,\\infty ),$\nand its complement is\n${\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q}=(-\\infty ,2].$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q} & =[-3,3]\\cap (2,\\infty ) \\\\  & =(2,3] \\\\ {\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q} & =((-\\infty ,-3)\\cup (3,\\infty ))\\cap (-\\infty ,2] \\\\  & =(-\\infty ,-3) \\\\ {T}_{P⇔Q} & =({T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q})\\cup ({\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q}) \\\\  & =(2,3]\\cup (-\\infty ,-3) \\\\  & =(-\\infty ,-3)\\cup (2,3].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-74cac60f-4eb1-54cb-950d-4d03ca15d20c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-74cac60f-4eb1-54cb-950d-4d03ca15d20c" :answer-field/id #uuid "74cac60f-4eb1-54cb-950d-4d03ca15d20c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9b4b0d88-2d4c-57d0-b244-861d5aa82dca" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5fb4114b-80de-58c7-a9c6-c2e4caceaeef" "answer-9b4b0d88-2d4c-57d0-b244-861d5aa82dca" "answer-10fd375b-d7d6-5467-8bdb-6f37bc432d98" "answer-9acebaf5-8307-528a-b69c-75e7d4aa4e69" "answer-c57b9858-4955-5a75-af05-c5a6fbbab5b5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5fb4114b-80de-58c7-a9c6-c2e4caceaeef" :answer/id #uuid "5fb4114b-80de-58c7-a9c6-c2e4caceaeef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-2,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9b4b0d88-2d4c-57d0-b244-861d5aa82dca" :answer/id #uuid "9b4b0d88-2d4c-57d0-b244-861d5aa82dca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-\\infty ,-3)\\cup (2,3]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-10fd375b-d7d6-5467-8bdb-6f37bc432d98" :answer/id #uuid "10fd375b-d7d6-5467-8bdb-6f37bc432d98" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-\\infty ,2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9acebaf5-8307-528a-b69c-75e7d4aa4e69" :answer/id #uuid "9acebaf5-8307-528a-b69c-75e7d4aa4e69" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c57b9858-4955-5a75-af05-c5a6fbbab5b5" :answer/id #uuid "c57b9858-4955-5a75-af05-c5a6fbbab5b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[-3,3]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186381672 :question/problem "Consider the following predicates.\n\n$\\,$ $A(x):$ $x\\in \\{-1,0,3,7\\}\\cap N.$ $\\,$ $B(x):$ $x\\in \\{3,7\\}.$ \n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to the biconditional predicate $A(x)⇔B(x)?$\n\nI. $x\\in \\{-1,0,3,7\\}\\cap N$ is equivalent to  $x\\in N.$\n\nII. $x\\in \\{-1,0,3,7\\}\\cap N$ if and only if $x\\in \\{3,7\\}.$\n\nIII. If $x\\in \\{-1,0,3,7\\}\\cap N$ then $x\\in \\{3,7\\},$ or if $x\\in \\{3,7\\}$ then $x\\in \\{-1,0,3,7\\}\\cap N.$" :question/worked-solution "A biconditional expression $P⇔Q≡(P⇒Q)∧(Q⇒P)$ can be read as shown below:\n\n- $P$ if and only if $Q$\n\n- $P$ is equivalent to $Q$\n\n- If $P$ then $Q,$ and if $Q$ then $P$\n\nSo, $A⇔B$ translates into the following sentences:\n\n- $x\\in \\{-1,0,3,7\\}\\cap N$ if and only if $x\\in \\{3,7\\}.$\n\n- $x\\in \\{-1,0,3,7\\}\\cap N$ is equivalent to $x\\in \\{3,7\\}.$\n\n- If $x\\in \\{-1,0,3,7\\}\\cap N$ then $x\\in \\{3,7\\},$ and if $x\\in \\{3,7\\}$ then $x\\in \\{-1,0,3,7\\}\\cap N.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198711 :question/problem "Consider the following predicates.\n\n$\\,$ $P(x):$ $x\\,|\\,8.$ $\\,$ $Q(x):$ $x$ is even.\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to the biconditional predicate $P(x)⇔Q(x)?$\n\nI. If $x\\,|\\,8$ then $x$ is even, or if $x$ is even then $x\\,|\\,8.$\n\nII. If $x\\,|\\,8$ then $x$ is even, and if $x$ is even then $x\\,|\\,8.$\n\nIII. $x\\,|\\,8$ if and only if $x$ is even." :question/worked-solution "A biconditional expression $P⇔Q≡(P⇒Q)∧(Q⇒P)$ can be read as shown below:\n\n- $P$ if and only if $Q$\n\n- $P$ is equivalent to $Q$\n\n- If $P$ then $Q,$ and if $Q$ then $P$\n\nSo, $A⇔B$ translates into the following sentences:\n\n- $x\\,|\\,8$ if and only if $x$ is even.\n\n- $x\\,|\\,8$ is equivalent to $x$ is even.\n\n- If $x\\,|\\,8$ then $x$ is even, and if $x$ is even then $x\\,|\\,8.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186194892 :answer-field/correct 17592186194897 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}]
